V4 is a **different failure mode**. It got past the old approval stall, then the fresh session hit threshold-driven compaction; that compaction exhausted its 180-second lifecycle and the run died without `STATUS=PASS`.  OpenClaw documents that threshold auto-compaction is enabled by default and can be disabled separately from overflow-recovery compaction, but we are **not changing that yet**. 

Next we determine whether `exec` actually happened before the transcript blew up.

### SHELL

```bash
OUT="$(cat "$HOME/.de_output_dir")"
RUN="$(find "$OUT" -maxdepth 1 -type d -name 'pan-actuator-v4-*' | sort | tail -1)"
SID="2e7e99b8-d5b4-4df8-a42e-417f994096af"
SESSION="$HOME/.openclaw/agents/main/sessions/$SID.jsonl"
SUM="$RUN/v4-transcript-summary.txt"

if [ ! -f "$SESSION" ]; then
  SESSION="$(grep -rl 'pan-actuator-v4' "$HOME/.openclaw/agents/main/sessions" 2>/dev/null | head -1)"
fi

python3 - "$RUN/agent.json" "$RUN/agent.stderr" "$SESSION" >"$SUM" <<'PY'
import json, os, sys

agent, stderr, session = sys.argv[1:4]

for p in (agent, stderr, session):
    if p and os.path.isfile(p):
        print(f"FILE {p} bytes={os.path.getsize(p)}")
    else:
        print(f"MISSING {p}")

print("\n=== AGENT RESULT SIGNALS ===")
for p in (agent, stderr):
    if not p or not os.path.isfile(p):
        continue
    text = open(p, errors="replace").read()
    hits = []
    for line in text.splitlines():
        if any(x in line.lower() for x in (
            "status=", "exec", "git -c", "error", "timeout",
            "compaction", "toolcall", "toolresult"
        )):
            hits.append(line[:700])
    for line in hits[-12:]:
        print(line)

print("\n=== SESSION STRUCTURE ===")
if session and os.path.isfile(session):
    for n, raw in enumerate(open(session, errors="replace"), 1):
        try:
            obj = json.loads(raw)
        except Exception:
            continue

        msg = obj.get("message", obj)
        if not isinstance(msg, dict):
            continue

        role = msg.get("role", "")
        content = msg.get("content", [])
        if not isinstance(content, list):
            content = [content]

        for item in content:
            if not isinstance(item, dict):
                continue

            typ = item.get("type", "")
            if typ == "thinking":
                continue

            if typ in ("toolCall", "tool_call"):
                name = item.get("name") or item.get("toolName")
                args = item.get("arguments") or item.get("input") or {}
                print(f"L{n} role={role} TOOLCALL name={name} args={str(args)[:500]}")

            elif typ in ("toolResult", "tool_result"):
                name = item.get("name") or item.get("toolName")
                val = item.get("content") or item.get("output") or item.get("result")
                print(f"L{n} role={role} TOOLRESULT name={name} result={str(val)[:500]}")

            elif typ == "text":
                val = str(item.get("text", ""))
                if "STATUS=" in val or "git" in val.lower() or "error" in val.lower():
                    print(f"L{n} role={role} TEXT={val[:500]}")

        stop = msg.get("stopReason") or msg.get("stop_reason")
        if stop:
            print(f"L{n} role={role} stopReason={stop}")
PY

echo "SUMMARY=$SUM"
tail -n 30 "$SUM"
```

This deliberately **does not print model thinking**. We only want the actuator anatomy: call, result, termination.

